+# Dynamic asteroid particle-effect NAP startup
+
+- Client: Release `03bfd87-git (20261017)`, SDL3/OpenGL 4.5, Mesa llvmpipe (software renderer), isolated Xephyr display.
+- Command: `lancer <isolated-client.ini> --new-game --render-particle-effects=on`.
+- Manifest: `lancer-pbr-qa-20261014`, SHA-256 `57af6496c39b4c35ebb32add550fd58ef00f5eb40f7658b7207a06fc99293652`. All 13 archive sizes and SHA-256 values matched the manifest and each archive passed `nexus-pack verify` immediately before launch.
+- No loose root `DATA` or `data` directory was present; Freelancer EXE configuration hashes matched staged `Data/NAP` files.
+- `Finished loading game data`, `UI: Interface loaded`, and `Entering system FP7_system` were reached. The previous three `Unknown entry particle_effect` warnings are absent.
+- FP7 intro does not expose a dynamic asteroid field. This verifies NAP parsing and startup only; the actual asteroid particle renderer has not received a visual runtime acceptance.
+- The software renderer reported dropped simulation ticks; this run is not performance evidence. Existing `explosion_impulse` and `MinSpecLOD` parser warnings remain outside this change.
+
+Relevant log lines:
+
+```text
+[Info: 21:22:06] Engine: Version: 03bfd87-git (20261017)
